{
  "causal_version": "2.3.0",
  "causal_version_note": "2.3.0 (EVR-1, labour data): the rates channel decides the sign of risk assets after a jobs report. JOBS_STRONG: yields up, USD up, equities and crypto DOWN only through the rates path (jobs-strong-rates); JOBS_WEAK: yields down, USD down, equities and crypto UP (jobs-weak-rates). The growth paths (jobs-*-growth, strength 18) are secondary: they never cancel the rates path (|net| / gross stays above conflict_net_ratio, so no asset is left unresolved) and lead only while a GROWTH_SCARE regime is active (regime multiplier 1.5, and the rates path's risk-asset leg is scaled to 0.25 by its exception), where weak data is bad news for equities and strong data a relief. Before 2.3.0 both branches netted to 'equities down' (growth 40/45 against rates 29.6). The event-risk layer reads the branches through causal.paths(trigger) with the regime context; the labour scenario templates name the triggers (event_exposure.json labor_release / claims_release). 2.2.0: classification principle of causal_triggers (note there).",
