    "note": "A trigger gives an event causal reach over many assets and a direction, so the text has to state it; an incidental word is not enough (causal 2.2.0). Each keyword rule is tried in order and the first match wins. Per rule: 'all' = keyword groups that must each be hit; 'direction_words' = one more required group, the word that gives the trigger its direction; 'none' = phrases that veto the rule; 'sources' = only these source ids (empty: any); 'authorities' = the sources whose own publication the trigger describes (ids or independence groups; their social accounts count through the group): for them the whole text is read and the group at 'actor_group' (the one naming the authority) is satisfied by the source itself; 'max_tier' = any other source must have at most this tier (sources.json source_tiers), otherwise the rule never fires for it; 'headline_only' = for any other source every group must be hit in the HEADLINE, not in the body. A rule with trigger null classifies the event (event_type, topic, linked 'assets') and gives it no trigger: no direction, no causal reach, no expected effects.",
